// =============================================================================
// 08: ROCK JAM — HIGHWAY RIFF & POWER ANTHEM (Key of D / Bm — 116 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// Driving 4/4 stadium rock backing track in the Key of D / Bm.
// Features overdriven power chord rhythm, pumping 8th-note bass, punchy rock drums,
// and full guitar soloing roadmap.
//
// 🎸 HOW TO JAM OVER KEY OF D / Bm:
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// • B Minor Pentatonic (Box 1, 7th Fret — The Ultimate Rock Box!):
//    e |--------------------------7--10--|  (B, D)
//    B |--------------------7--10--------|  (F#, A)
//    G |----------------7--9-------------|  (D, E)
//    D |----------7--9-------------------|  (A, B)
//    A |----7--9-------------------------|  (E, F#)
//    E |--7--10--------------------------|  (B, D)
//
// • Essential Rock Lead Moves:
//   1. The Classic Unison Bend:
//      Fret 10 on B string (A note) while fretting 7 on high E string (B note).
//      Bend the B string up a whole step with your ring finger until both notes scream!
//   2. The Chuck Berry / AC-DC Double-Stop:
//      Barre frets 7 on G & B strings with your index finger, strike together,
//      hammer onto fret 9 of D string, resolve to fret 7 on G!
//   3. Major Pentatonic Sweetness (D Major):
//      Slide into 11th fret on G string (F# note) for soaring melodic Southern rock.
//
// 🎼 HARMONIC ROADMAP:
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Track 1: [Bm] -> [G] -> [D] -> [A]  (vi - IV - I - V Anthem Rock)
// Track 2: [D]  -> [C] -> [G] -> [D]  (I - bVII - IV - I Classic 70s Rock)
//
// 🎛️ CONTROLS (<leader> = Space in Neovim):
//   <leader>ml : :StrudelLaunch (Connect to Strudel engine)
//   <leader>mp : :StrudelToggle (Play / Pause backing track)
//   <leader>mu : :StrudelUpdate (APPLY CHANGES LIVE — Press after uncommenting!)
//   gcc        : Toggle comment on a line (1 tap to introduce/mute a layer)
// =============================================================================


// =============================================================================
// ⚡ TRACK 1: "HIGHWAY DRIVE" (Driving Anthem Rock — Key of D / Bm — 116 CPM)
// =============================================================================
// LIVE-BUILDING FLOW:
//   Starts with ONLY Layer 1 active (crunchy power chords).
//   Introduce layers live as your solo builds up:
//   Line 53: Pumping Bass | Line 56: Driving Hats | Line 59: Snare | Line 62: Kick

stack(
  // [Step 1 - ACTIVE AT START] Overdriven Rhythm Chords (Bm -> G -> D -> A)
  note("<[b2,fs3,b3] [g2,d3,g3] [d3,a3,d4] [a2,e3,a3]>")
    .s("sawtooth")
    .lpf(1600)
    .decay(0.9)
    .gain(0.42),

  // [Step 2 - BASS] Pumping 8th-Note Rock Bassline (Press gcc here)
  // note("<b1*8 g1*8 d2*8 a1*8>").s("sawtooth").lpf(550).decay(0.35).gain(0.65),

  // [Step 3 - HI-HAT] Driving 8th-note hats with velocity dynamic pulse (Press gcc here)
  // s("hh*8").gain(sine.range(0.28, 0.55).fast(4)),

  // [Step 4 - SNARE] Cracking rock backbeat snare on 2 & 4 (Press gcc here)
  // s("~ sd ~ sd").room(0.35).gain(0.8),

  // [Step 5 - KICK] Heavy driving kick pattern (Press gcc here to anchor!)
  // s("bd [~ bd] bd ~").gain(0.85),

  // [Step 6 - CRASH] Big cymbal crash on downbeat of cycle (Press gcc here!)
  // s("cr ~ ~ ~").slow(4).gain(0.4),

  // [Step 7 - LEAD SYNTH] Ambient arena synth hook (Press gcc here!)
  // note("<[fs4,b4,d5] [g4,b4,d5] [fs4,a4,d5] [e4,a4,cs5]>").s("square").lpf(1300).delay(0.3).room(0.6).gain(0.28),
).cpm(116)


